    r: ['Correct. Blood in the gut is a large protein load that bacteria turn into ammonia.', 'Correct. Constipation keeps ammonia in the colon longer to be absorbed.', 'Correct. Hypokalemia increases ammonia production.', 'Correct. Infection is a common trigger.', 'Incorrect. That is lactulose’s goal — it lowers ammonia.', 'Incorrect. Carbohydrate isn’t a trigger; a high-protein load is.', 'Incorrect. Pruritus comes from bilirubin and doesn’t affect the brain.'],
